    {
      "indicator_id": "fish_contact_fragmentation_meso",
      "phenomenon_id": "school_fission_stretch",
      "name": "Fish contact-graph fragmentation index",
      "scale": "meso",
      "description": "Mesoscale fragmentation of the fish interaction graph, measured as one minus the fraction of fish in the largest connected component formed by native contact edges at the same step.",
      "mathematical_definition": "For each run_id r and step t, let V_{r,t} = {i : role_i = 'fish' at (r,t)}. Build an undirected graph G_{r,t} = (V_{r,t}, E_{r,t}), where E_{r,t} contains an unordered pair {a,b} if and only if a,b are in V_{r,t} and there exists a contacts row at (r,t) with {agent_id, partner_id} = {a,b}; duplicate edges are collapsed. Let components C_1,...,C_k be the connected components of G_{r,t}, and let M_{r,t} = max_m |C_m|. Define fragmentation F_{r,t} = 1 - M_{r,t}/|V_{r,t}| when |V_{r,t}| > 0; if |V_{r,t}| = 0, F_{r,t} is undefined.",
      "units": "dimensionless",
      "computation_notes": "Computed per run_id and step as a snapshot of the native contact edge list. Vertices are fish agents present in agent_states at that step; contacts rows are retained only when both endpoints are fish at the same run_id and step. Edges are treated as undirected and deduplicated. Missing or sentinel identifiers are excluded. No external group IDs are introduced; connected components are derived only from recorded edges.",
      "required_data": {
        "agent_states": [
          "run_id",
          "step",
          "agent_id",
          "role"
        ],
        "contacts": [
          "run_id",
          "step",
          "agent_id",
          "partner_id"
        ]
      },
      "required": {
        "agent_states": [
          "step",
          "agent_id",
          "role"
        ],
        "contacts": [
          "step",
          "agent_id",
          "partner_id"
        ]
      },
      "config": {},
      "python_code": "import numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef _fragmentation(fish_ids, edges):\n    n = len(fish_ids)\n    if n == 0:\n        return np.nan\n    parent = {i: i for i in fish_ids}\n    size = {i: 1 for i in fish_ids}\n\n    def find(x):\n        root = x\n        while parent[root] != root:\n            root = parent[root]\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            p = parent[x]\n            parent[x] = root\n            x = p\n        return root\n\n    def union(a, b):\n        ra = find(a)\n        rb = find(b)\n        if ra == rb:\n            return\n        if size[ra] < size[rb]:\n            ra, rb = rb, ra\n        parent[rb] = ra\n        size[ra] += size[rb]\n\n    for a, b in edges:\n        if a in parent and b in parent:\n            union(a, b)\n\n    counts = {}\n    for i in fish_ids:\n        r = find(i)\n        counts[r] = counts.get(r, 0) + 1\n    largest = max(counts.values())\n    return 1.0 - float(largest) / float(n)\n\n\ndef compute_indicator(data, config):\n    agents = data['agent_states']\n    contacts = data['contacts']\n\n    role = agents['role'].astype(str).str.strip()\n    fish_mask = role.eq('fish') & agents['agent_id'].notna()\n    fish_df = agents.loc[fish_mask, ['step', 'agent_id']].copy()\n    if len(fish_df):\n        fish_df['step'] = fish_df['step'].astype('int64')\n        fish_df['agent_id'] = fish_df['agent_id'].astype('int64')\n\n    c = contacts[['step', 'agent_id', 'partner_id']].dropna(\n        subset=['step', 'agent_id', 'partner_id']\n    ).copy()\n    if len(c):\n        c['step'] = c['step'].astype('int64')\n        c['agent_id'] = c['agent_id'].astype('int64')\n        c['partner_id'] = c['partner_id'].astype('int64')\n\n    fish_by_step = {}\n    for step, g in fish_df.groupby('step', sort=False):\n        fish_by_step[step] = set(g['agent_id'].tolist())\n\n    edges_by_step = {}\n    for step, a, b in c[['step', 'agent_id', 'partner_id']].itertuples(\n        index=False, name=None\n    ):\n        edges_by_step.setdefault(step, []).append((a, b))\n\n    all_steps = sorted(agents['step'].dropna().astype('int64').unique().tolist())\n    values = {}\n    for step in all_steps:\n        values[step] = _fragmentation(\n            fish_by_step.get(step, set()),\n            edges_by_step.get(step, []),\n        )\n\n    series = pd.Series(\n        values,\n        name='fish_contact_fragmentation_meso',\n        dtype='float64',\n    )\n    series.index.name = 'step'\n    return series.sort_index()\n",
      "implementation_status": "implemented",
      "failure_reason": null,
      "node_id": "fish_contact_fragmentation_meso",
      "code_file": "\\\\?\\E:\\work\\成果\\发表论文\\Nature Communication\\abms_lab\\full_pipeline\\results\\live_fish_20261107\\internal\\stage1\\builds\\84e6aaa8ed4e0764c65dfbc60067eabac5a26619d330815bbc513df48ba7e479\\indicator_code\\fish_contact_fragmentation_meso.py",
