    {
      "indicator_id": "fish_school_elongation_macro",
      "phenomenon_id": "school_fission_stretch",
      "name": "Fish school elongation index",
      "scale": "macro",
      "description": "Macroscopic anisotropy of the fish school's spatial distribution at each step, measured from the principal eigenvalues of the fish position covariance matrix as an overall stretching indicator.",
      "mathematical_definition": "For each run_id r and step t, let P_{r,t} = {(x_i(t), y_i(t)) : role_i = 'fish' with finite coordinates} and N = |P_{r,t}|. If N >= 2, define the centroid μ = (1/N) Σ_{p in P_{r,t}} p and covariance C = (1/N) Σ_{p in P_{r,t}} (p-μ)(p-μ)^T. Let λ1 >= λ2 >= 0 be the eigenvalues of C. Define elongation E_{r,t} = sqrt(λ1/λ2) when λ2 > 0; if λ2 = 0 or N < 2, E_{r,t} is undefined.",
      "units": "dimensionless",
      "computation_notes": "Computed per run_id and step on fish positions only; shark positions are excluded. The covariance uses denominator N (population form) to preserve the stated definition. Each sampled step is a separate snapshot; no temporal smoothing or event window is applied. Missing or non-finite coordinates are excluded before computing the centroid and covariance. No group IDs or hidden clustering are used.",
      "required_data": {
        "agent_states": [
          "run_id",
          "step",
          "agent_id",
          "role",
          "x",
          "y"
        ]
      },
      "required": {
        "agent_states": [
          "run_id",
          "step",
          "role",
          "x",
          "y"
        ]
      },
      "config": {},
      "python_code": "import numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef compute_indicator(data, config):\n    _ = config\n    df = data['agent_states']\n    cols = ['run_id', 'step', 'role', 'x', 'y']\n    missing = [c for c in cols if c not in df.columns]\n    if missing:\n        raise KeyError(f'agent_states missing required columns: {missing}')\n    d = df.loc[:, cols].copy()\n    d = d[d['role'].astype(str) == 'fish'].copy()\n    d['x'] = pd.to_numeric(d['x'], errors='coerce')\n    d['y'] = pd.to_numeric(d['y'], errors='coerce')\n    d['step'] = pd.to_numeric(d['step'], errors='coerce')\n    d = d.dropna(subset=['run_id', 'step', 'x', 'y'])\n    d = d[np.isfinite(d['x']) & np.isfinite(d['y']) & np.isfinite(d['step'])]\n    d = d[d['step'] == np.floor(d['step'])].copy()\n    d['step'] = d['step'].astype('int64')\n    rows = []\n    if len(d):\n        for (run_id, step), g in d.groupby(['run_id', 'step'], sort=False):\n            n = len(g)\n            if n < 2:\n                val = np.nan\n            else:\n                x = g['x'].to_numpy(dtype=float)\n                y = g['y'].to_numpy(dtype=float)\n                dx = x - x.mean()\n                dy = y - y.mean()\n                cxx = float(np.mean(dx * dx))\n                cyy = float(np.mean(dy * dy))\n                cxy = float(np.mean(dx * dy))\n                tr = cxx + cyy\n                disc = float(np.sqrt(max((cxx - cyy) ** 2 + 4.0 * cxy * cxy, 0.0)))\n                lam1 = (tr + disc) / 2.0\n                lam2 = (tr - disc) / 2.0\n                if lam2 > 0.0:\n                    val = float(np.sqrt(lam1 / lam2))\n                else:\n                    val = np.nan\n            rows.append((run_id, int(step), val))\n    if not rows:\n        return pd.Series(dtype=float, name='fish_school_elongation_macro').rename_axis('step')\n    res = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=['run_id', 'step', 'fish_school_elongation_macro'])\n    run_ids = res['run_id'].unique()\n    if len(run_ids) == 1:\n        out = res.set_index('step')['fish_school_elongation_macro'].sort_index()\n        out.index.name = 'step'\n        out.name = 'fish_school_elongation_macro'\n        return out\n    out = res.pivot(index='step', columns='run_id', values='fish_school_elongation_macro').sort_index()\n    out.index.name = 'step'\n    return out\n",
      "implementation_status": "implemented",
      "failure_reason": null,
      "node_id": "fish_school_elongation_macro",
      "code_file": "\\\\?\\E:\\work\\成果\\发表论文\\Nature Communication\\abms_lab\\full_pipeline\\results\\live_fish_20261107\\internal\\stage1\\builds\\84e6aaa8ed4e0764c65dfbc60067eabac5a26619d330815bbc513df48ba7e479\\indicator_code\\fish_school_elongation_macro.py",
